CC0 asks for nothing. Kenney is credited here, in the game's Credits page
and in this paragraph anyway, because the game would not look or sound
like anything without that work.

## Explosions — Wikimedia Commons, public domain

Two recordings, trimmed to the bang, with the low end lifted; the
knockout rumble is the first of them low-passed and slowed, so it is the
same real blast heard through a wall.

| File | Source | By |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `game/assets/sounds/explosion_near.ogg`, `explosion_deep.ogg` | [Explosion 10.ogg](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Explosion_10.ogg) | tcpp |
| `game/assets/sounds/explosion_far.ogg` | [Explosion-LS100155.ogg](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Explosion-LS100155.ogg) | Fg2 |

Public domain asks for nothing. Both are credited here and on the game's
Credits page anyway.

## Building kits — Silicon23, MIT

<https://github.com/Silicon23/MoreChineseStructures>

The 28 stampable Minecraft builds in `game/src/structures_imported.gd`,
generated from the structure-block `.nbt` files in `kits/downloads/`.
Per-build attribution is in `kits/manifest.json` and is shown in the
game's Credits page.

