## Generated from the above

`game/assets/ui/weapons/w*.png` are hotbar icons rendered from the Kenney
Blaster Kit models by `game/tests/weapon_icons.gd`, so they carry the same
CC0 terms. `game/src/structures_imported.gd` is generated from the MIT
kits by `game/tests/import_structures.gd` and carries theirs.

## Minecraft maps

`maps/` holds Anvil region files for four small worlds, used to exercise
the `.mca` importer. They are original builds, not redistributed content
from anyone else's world.

Minecraft is a trademark of Mojang Studios. This project is not
affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to Mojang or Microsoft in any
way. It reads the Anvil file format; it ships no Minecraft code, assets or
data.

## Engine

Godot Engine, MIT — <https://godotengine.org>. Not vendored here; the
build downloads it (see `Dockerfile`).

## Art that used to be here and is not

Four purchased voxel animal packs and the "Little People in Voxel"
characters were once committed as extracted `.glb`/`.obj` files. Using
purchased assets in a game is ordinarily fine; putting the raw meshes in a
public repository is redistribution, and nothing in those licences allowed
it. They were removed in full, along with the creature and character
entries that referenced them, before this repository was published.
